      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2t-1,\\,\\,\\,y=2-{t}^{2},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14111253/assets/5cd074670c05cea0c68db75c7e1a57309c017c97556e976f2db4c3bf1b358a85.png)",
